the princes.{Achashdarpenaya,} rendered lieutenants in Es 3:12, etc.,
probably {chief satraps or viceroys} from the Persian {achash}
great, eminent, and {sitrab}, a satrap.

Nebuchadnezzar.Nebuchadnezzar was certainly the grandfather of Belshazzar;
but the term father in Hebrew and Chaldee is frequently used
to denote a progenitor, or ancestor, however remote.

for.It is now 2,387 years since Daniel had this vision; and the
utter desolation of the sanctuary had continued 1,764 years;
and no doubt the end of 2,300 years is not far distant.
